{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1hiwvocAX9YtQBppu4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the second-publish crash: every publish after the first now returns 201, and the tests pass. The changes aren't committed. The cause, the fix and which parts of your colleague's note applied are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Cause:** Each publish saves the story with its 3 most similar stories, and each of those has a score. `similarity()` returns that score as a Python float (from `round(...)`), and DynamoDB won't accept floats in an item. On the first publish the table was empty, so there were no scores and no floats, which is why it worked. Every later publish has at least one score. Even completely unrelated stories get `0.0`, which is still a float, so every publish after the first fails with a 500.\n\n**Fix (`src/app.py`):**\n- **`to_dynamo()`:** a new function that turns every float anywhere in the item into a `Decimal` just before `put_item`. That keeps the exact 4-decimal score, and a float added to the item later can't cause this again.\n- **Input checks:** a request that isn't a JSON object, or that has `slug`, `title`, `body` or `tags` of the wrong type, now gets a 400. Before, it could also put a float into the item or crash with a 500.\n\n**Tests (`tests/test_publish.py`):** the new tests fill the table before publishing, including three publishes in a row through `handler()` and the zero-score case. All 8 tests pass with the fix; with the original `app.py`, 7 of them fail.\n\n**From the colleague's note:**\n- **Used:** the diagnosis, converting computed values just before the write, and filling the table before testing a write.\n- **Not used:** their integer-percentage fix, since it would round 0.4667 to 47 and change what the stored score means.\n- **Not done:** \"publish twice against a real table\", because your ground rules rule out external services. I tested against the repo's fake table, which rejects floats the same way boto3 does. It's still worth doing two real publishes in a non-production environment before the next deploy.\n\nNo existing data needs fixing: every write that would have stored a float failed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1631,"cache_read_input_tokens":29384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1631},"output_tokens":658,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ef0a5df-d47f-4b2c-9506-d985e4d0328f","uuid":"5e758c6d-85f7-48ed-b313-5af03353876a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:14:03.756Z","request_id":"req_011CgS1higopKBpYthWrgs2o"}
